 ## Background
-This method was introduced in "Loss-Guided Density Control and Efficient Backward Optimisation for Compact Gaussian Splatting" [S1, unofficial]. It builds upon the standard 3D Gaussian Splatting densification process by adding a post-densification pruning step that uses opacity gradients and training loss to guide the removal of primitives [S1, unofficial].
+This method was introduced in "Loss-Guided Density Control and Efficient Backward Optimisation for Compact Gaussian Splatting" [S2, unofficial]. It builds upon the standard 3D Gaussian Splatting densification process by adding a post-densification pruning step that uses opacity gradients and training loss to guide the removal of primitives [S2, unofficial].
 
